dialogue silas
  node root silas "The clerk. Silas Cray, of Cray & Co. I ship things, I insure things, and now and then I collect things. You're after the last berth on the Marrow. I've bought it."
    > "I still haven't come round." if silas_offer = true and not silas_refused -> refuse
    > "The berth isn't yours to sell." -> keep
    > "What do you want for it?" -> compass
    > "Excuse me." -> bye
  node keep silas "Not to sell. To keep. I have a receipt, and Bramwick has a ledger, and between them it's mine. Men who want to sail always come round."
    > "Then I'll swim." if seen:silas.compass -> swim_offer
    > "Then I'll swim." if not seen:silas.compass -> swim
    > "What would it take to come round?" -> compass
    > "We'll see." -> bye
  node compass silas "Your compass. Your grandfather made it, your father hid it, and you carry it about like a pocket watch that's lost its nerve. Give it to me and the berth is yours."
    set silas_offer
    > "Why do you want it?" -> why
    > "No." -> refuse
  node why silas "Because it points somewhere, and I collect things that point. Other men collect beetles. Mine is the more profitable hobby."
    > "You'd take it anyway." -> hard
    > "No." -> refuse
  node hard silas "Take? Taking leaves a record, and I'm very fond of the ledger as it is. No, I'll wait. Men who want to sail always come round."
    > "Then I'll swim." -> swim_offer
    > "We'll see." -> bye
  node swim silas "Swim, then. The Straits are lovely this time of year. Ask your father."
    set silas_refused
    note cray_berth "Silas Cray has bought the last berth on the Marrow, and means to keep it. I told him I'd swim. He found that very funny."
  node swim_offer silas "Swim, then. The Straits are lovely this time of year. Ask your father."
    set silas_refused
    note cray_offer "Cray offered me the last berth for my father's compass. He knows it points somewhere useful, and he would rather buy it than take it. I said no."
  node refuse silas "No. Your father said that too. Such a family for one-syllable answers. Good night, clerk."
    set silas_refused
    note cray_offer "Cray offered me the last berth for my father's compass. He knows it points somewhere useful, and he would rather buy it than take it. I said no."
  node bye silas "Run along. The bell won't wait, and neither will I. Well. I will. I'm very patient."
